{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"isotropic and anisotropic thermal conductivity isotropic and anisotropic thermal conductivity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity.md","fileName":"Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Thermophysical Material Characterization]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermophysical Material Characterization","Finite Element Thermal Modeling","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"isotropic and anisotropic thermal conductivity isotropic and anisotropic thermal conductivity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity.md","fileName":"Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity","heading":"Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An isotropic material uses the same thermal conductivity in every direction. An anisotropic material requires directional values, so conductive heat flux need not align simply with a scalar conductivity times the temperature gradient.\n\nTransversely isotropic materials share properties within a plane but differ normal to it, while orthotropic materials have three distinct values along orthogonal axes. Rolled sheet and layered structures therefore require orientation-aware inputs in [[Finite Element Thermal Modeling|finite-element models]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermophysical Material Characterization","Finite Element Thermal Modeling","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"isotropic and anisotropic thermal conductivity isotropic and anisotropic thermal conductivity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity.md","fileName":"Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Isotropic and Anisotropic Thermal Conductivity","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermophysical Material Characterization","Finite Element Thermal Modeling","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}